  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the health system towards Universal Health Coverage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention intends to enhance the governance capacities of the ministries of Health, Economy, and Public Administration for an efficient management of the health system, and to facilitate access to quality and inclusive health services and essential medical products. Improving access of citizens, especially those in most vulnerable situations, to quality healthcare services will pave the way for Universal Health Coverage (UHC). The approach includes: i) building capacities on health planning, budgeting and supervision, based on a stronger information system, ii) improving policies and regulation mechanisms for a more equitable and regular access to essential medicines and their efficient management, and iii) ensuring the alignment of the national regulatory framework with international standards, as well as improving the physical conditions of the services (medicines management and healthcare workforce distribution) and the skills development of the health workforce. The action is aligned with the national plans on health and builds on lessons learned from previous EU-funded actions. The action should be implemented through a contribution agreement with an entrusted entity on the strengthening of the health system (EUR 10M), and a top-up grant to the ongoing programme on maternal and child health (EUR 1M).</narrative>
  </description>
